  "verbalization": "Nimustine is shown to have a target relationship with Sucrose porin, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including (1S,2R,3S,4R,5S)-8-Azabicyclo[3.2.1]Octane-2,3,4,5-Tetrol and (1S,3R,4R,6R,7R,8S,9R,10R,13S,16R)-5,5,9,14-tetramethyltetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,8]hexadec-14-ene-3,4,6,7,9,16-hexol. These compounds are all implicated in targeting the Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein, suggesting a potential pathway through which Nimustine may influence the protein. The evidence indicates that Nimustine indirectly affects the Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein via the Sucrose porin, which serves as a common intermediate in multiple target pathways. The scores from the different paths suggest a consistent but not absolute relationship, highlighting the need for further experimental validation. The mechanisms appear to involve the modulation of a shared target, but the exact role of Sucrose porin in this process remains to be elucidated.",
